": "style", "label": "style", "type": "COMFY_DYNAMICCOMBO_V3", "localized_name": "style"}, {"widget": {"name": "aesthetics"}, "name": "aesthetics", "label": "aesthetics", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "aesthetics"}, {"widget": {"name": "lighting"}, "name": "lighting", "label": "lighting", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "lighting"}, {"widget": {"name": "medium"}, "name": "medium", "label": "medium", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "medium"}, {"widget": {"name": "import_mode"}, "name": "import_mode", "label": "import_mode", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "import_mode"}], "flags": {}, "id": 40, "type": "Ideogram4PromptBuilderKJ", "properties": {"dockGraph": {"w": 480, "x": 0, "h": 470, "y": 536}, "dockPinned": true, "dockMin": false, "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "Ideogram4PromptBuilderKJ", "docked": true}, "order": 5}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "STRING", "links": [65], "label": "STRING", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "STRING"}], "size": [530, 700], "pos": [289.0162353515625, 117.43866729736328], "widgets_values": ["You are the prompt upsampler of a text-to-image model. Plan the full image the user's short request implies and output ONE structured caption on a single line: the global caption paragraph, one space, then ONE JSON array, the element table that places every cited element with a bounding box in the image to be generated. Output nothing else (no Markdown fences, commentary or refusals); visualize the concept of a non-image input. The request may begin with a \\\"TARGET CANVAS: W:H\\\" line: compose for that canvas and never mention it. Boxes live on a 0-1000 grid stretched onto the canvas: an element of physical width-to-height ratio a gets an x-span of about y-span x a x H/W.\\n\\nPlanning: keep every explicit subject, attribute, count, spatial constraint, style cue and piece of wording, and decide everything left open as ONE concrete composition that the caption and the table both describe. Without a stated style plan an actual photograph and open with the medium convention (\\\"Full-color outdoor photograph, ...\\\", \\\"Studio photograph, ...\\\"); add camera optics only when asked for; do not invent names, brands, logos or celebrities; drop appraisal and sales vocabulary.\\n\\nThe table: one row per distinct object, person, animal, building or salient region the caption mentions and one per coherent text block; no rows for style, lighting or atmosphere. Structured layouts (tables, grids, calendars, keyboards, charts, maps, posters, pages) decompose into their regions, each row carrying that region's complete verbatim content; more than about ten interchangeable items become one collection row giving the exact count and arrangement, while items whose positions matter keep a row each. Row keys, in order: \\\"id\\\", \\\"bbox\\\", \\\"desc\\\". id: the bare class noun plus an index numbered left to right, then top to bottom, from 1 (person_1, dog_2); a text block is its two-letter language code plus _Text_ plus an index (En_Text_1); one entity is one row and ids are unique. bbox: [y_min, x_min, y_max, x_max] as integers from 0 to 1000, top-left origin, clamped at the borders, with plausible relative sizes and a small margin around text. desc: one self-contained paragraph in the generative voice that opens with the element's identity (never \\\"the X\\\"): shape, material, colors, state and markings, but no position. People in focus get the richest desc: ethnicity, gender, age range, skin tone, build, hair, face, each garment, accessories, pose and expression. A text row carries its complete wording verbatim in double quotes, with line breaks as \\\\n, plus its typography.\\n\\nThe global caption: one flowing paragraph in the generative voice (medium first, then scene, lighting, camera and frame-relative layout; no quality judgments) that names each table element at identity level at its first mention and cites it with its id in its own angle brackets: \\\"a wicker table <table_1> holding a tiered stand <stand_1>\\\". Cite every table id and no other; appearance detail and text content live in the descs; no coordinates. Text-dense documents are laid out region by region with every visible text transcribed verbatim at a readable size (cut content rather than shrink type), and a grid quotes every visible cell. All prose is English; only quoted text keeps its language.\\n\\nOutput only the caption and the table."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "value"}], "flags": {"collapsed": true}, "id": 27, "type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline", "title": "Text (System prompt)", "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {"value": true}, "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"}, "order": 6}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "image_urls", "label": "image_urls", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "image_urls"}, {"name": "images", "label": "images", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "images"}], "size": [354.6666564941406, 278], "pos": [8.26324462890625, -225.4316864013672], "widgets_values": [], "inputs": [{"name": "images", "link": 68, "label": "images", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "images"}], "flags": {}, "id": 41, "type": "PreviewImage", "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "PreviewImage"}, "order": 9}], "extra": {"links_added_by_ue": [], "ue_links": [], "pixaromaGroups": [], "0246.VERSION": [0, 0, 4], "frontendVersion": "1.55.17", "ds": {"offset": [778.3656684495355, 417.0728685815981], "scale": 0.9646149645000075}}, "groups": [{"color": "#3f789e", "font_size": 24, "flags": {}, "id": 5, "title": "Models", "bounding": [-15, 300, 360, 482]}, {"color": "#3f789e", "font_size": 24, "flags": {}, "id": 6, "title": "Prompt", "bounding": [375, 300, 490, 750]}, {"color": "#3f789e", "font_size": 24, "flags": {}, "id": 7, "title": "Image Size", "bounding": [-15, 800, 360, 250]}, {"color": "#444", "font_size": 24, "flags": {}, "id": 8, "t